Heart Disease Prediction using Machine Learning
📌 Task Objective

The objective of this task is to build a machine learning model that predicts whether a person is at risk of heart disease based on clinical and demographic features.

This project was completed as part of the AI/ML Engineering Internship at DevelopersHub Corporation to demonstrate practical skills in:

Binary classification

Data preprocessing

Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

Model evaluation using medical performance metrics

Feature importance interpretation

📊 Dataset Used

Dataset Name: Heart Failure Prediction Dataset
Source: Kaggle

The dataset contains medical and physiological attributes of patients.

Features:

Age

Sex

ChestPainType

RestingBP

Cholesterol

FastingBS

RestingECG

MaxHR

ExerciseAngina

Oldpeak

ST_Slope

Target Variable:

HeartDisease

0 → No Heart Disease

1 → Heart Disease

The dataset includes both numerical and categorical features. Categorical variables were encoded using One-Hot Encoding before model training.

🤖 Models Applied
1️⃣ Logistic Regression

Logistic Regression was selected as the primary model because:

It is suitable for binary classification problems.

It provides interpretable coefficients.

It performs well on structured medical datasets.

Preprocessing Steps:

Checked and handled missing values

Applied One-Hot Encoding for categorical features

Split dataset into 80% training and 20% testing sets

Applied StandardScaler for feature scaling

📈 Model Evaluation Metrics

The model was evaluated using:

Accuracy

Precision

Recall

F1-Score

Confusion Matrix

ROC Curve

ROC-AUC Score

🏆 Key Results and Findings
📊 Performance Results:

Accuracy: 85.3%

ROC-AUC Score: 0.92

Classification Performance:

Precision (Heart Disease): 0.90

Recall (Heart Disease): 0.84

F1-Score: 0.87

Interpretation:

The model correctly classifies 85% of patients.

The ROC-AUC score of 0.92 indicates excellent discrimination ability.

The model successfully identifies 84% of heart disease cases.

In medical AI, recall for the positive class (disease detection) is particularly important, and the model performs strongly in this regard.

Important Predictive Features:

ChestPainType

ST_Slope

ExerciseAngina

Oldpeak

MaxHR

These features showed strong influence in predicting heart disease risk.

